  It's a no-brainer for my wizards.  Use the mithril to survive now.
Immediate survival is the first step to becoming an unstoppable spell
casting machine later.

  A quick wizmode test shows only 10% failure on the spell of magic
missile when wearing mithril:   In:17 Wi:11 Pw:7(7) AC:4  Exp:1.

  Of course, at XL:1 you'll only be averaging 3.5 damage per hit with
the spell of magic missile.  And Pw:7 isn't enough to cast magic missile
even once.

  So for an XL:1 wizard mithril is a no-brainer.  Heck, for an XL:1
wizard almost any non-cursed body armor is a no-brainer.

>Which is more important - the AC increase or the
>decrease in casting accuracy that comes with it?  
                     ^^^^^^^^
                     success

  Improved AC is more important early on.  Early wizards don't have
enough mana or (generally) the right spells (magic missile) to survive
as pure spell casters.  Better AC works on all monsters (important when
mobbed) and doesn't run out.

  Elven mithril is only two points better than studded leather armor.
Once enough accessory armor (boots, helm, gloves, shield) has been found
to make up the difference switching to studded leather is easy.  

  Note also that checking every non-cursed plain/studded leather armor
found greatly improves the chance of finding some pre-enchanted.   Don't
forget to check the armor left by leather golems.  +4 leather armor
(which I have gotten from killing leather golems) is a no-brainer for
almost any early character.


